    "user_request_original": "Perform one bounded TMM thickness optimization for an exactly 20-layer planar stack. Use the fixed material sequence from the incident side: HfO2 / Fused Silica / HfO2 / Fused Silica / HfO2 / Fused Silica / HfO2 / Fused Silica / HfO2 / Fused Silica / HfO2 / Fused Silica / HfO2 / Fused Silica / HfO2 / Fused Silica / HfO2 / Fused Silica / HfO2 / Fused Silica. Optimize only the physical thickness of each finite layer within the user-declared bounds. Do not optimize material identity or layer count in this route. Optimize a 20-layer defect-cavity dielectric stack on fused silica substrate with air incidence. Material sequence: SiO2|HfO2|SiO2|HfO2|SiO2|HfO2|SiO2|HfO2|SiO2|HfO2(cavity)|SiO2|HfO2|SiO2|HfO2|SiO2|HfO2|SiO2|HfO2|SiO2|HfO2. All 20 layer thicknesses are optimizable variables. Initialize layer 10 (HfO2 cavity) with uniform random distribution bounded to [220, 320] nm. Initialize all other layers with uniform random distribution bounded to [100, 400] nm. Evaluate spectral performance over 300-450 nm (target: high reflectance) and 1000-1700 nm (target: high transmittance) bands at normal incidence. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer with maximum 500 iterations. Report best_target_score, valid_candidates count, tightest_margin, and thicknesses_nm for all candidates. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 300-450 nm, 1000-1700 nm. soft objectives: high transmission in 1000-1700 nm; high reflection in 300-450 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: reflection in 1000-1700 nm; transmission in 300-450 nm. manufacturing constraints: Maximum total layer count of 30.",
